.TH JSON_VALID 3
.SH NAME
json_valid \- check a JSON text
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <json.h>
.P
.BI "int json_valid(const char* " x ", size_t " n ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION

.BR json_valid ()
tells if the n bytes at x are exactly one JSON value as RFC 8259 defines it. The reader json_read_tree(3) takes much more and does not tell when it gave up.
.SH RETURN VALUE
1 if valid, 0 if not.
.SH SEE ALSO
json_parse_text(3)
